{:id "0056-lab-tour"
 :title "Lab tour: a demo of under a minute that plays itself (types, reads back, dresses, dims the lights), with captions, and stops the moment you touch a key"
 :lupa/deps #{"0055-lab-default-feel"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "Ben asked: 'is there a demo to run and look at'. The lab only shows
        what it can do to someone who knows what to type. Add a tour: a
        scripted minute in which the lab types into its own text box,
        with a caption for each scene, so a visitor (or Ben, skimming) can
        watch the held note, a read-back, the same line in another style,
        dress and its gold, and the lights going down, then is handed the
        keyboard. The tour is data played through the lab's ordinary
        paths, so what it shows is what typing does."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/tour.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/tour_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "public/lab/index.html"
         "resources/site/index.html" "test/halfahead/dev/site_test.clj"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "halfahead.lab.tour (.cljc, pure): the tour as data and its clock.
          script -> a vector of scenes, each {:caption string :steps
            [step ...]}; a step is one of
              {:do :clear}                         empty the text box
              {:do :type :text s :ms-per-key n}    type s, a key every n ms
              {:do :wait :ms n}
              {:do :style :style kw}               pick a named style
              {:do :reveal :level n}               raise the reveal level to n
              {:do :read-back :wpm n}              start a read-back at n wpm
              {:do :until-read}                    wait until the read-back is over
              {:do :light :over s :ms n}           sweep the pointer's light
                                                   across the phrase s over n ms
          The scenes, in order, with these captions and texts (the
          foreman's draft of the product voice; change nothing):
            1 'It starts like any chat box.'
              reveal 0; style Plain; type 'Nothing to see here. Just
              typing.' (70 ms a key); wait 900
            2 'What matters can stay gold.'
              clear; reveal 1 (still paper); style Elegant; type 'This is
              *the one thing* that matters (trust me).' (60 ms a key);
              wait 900; light over 'the one thing' for 2400 ms; wait 400
            3 'Hold a letter, and it holds the note.'
              clear; type 'I loooove this ' (110 ms a key); wait 3200
            4 'Then the lights go down. Some words know what they are.'
              clear; reveal 3; style Plain; type 'We shipped it. Finally! '
              (90 ms a key); wait 1800
            5 'Ctrl+Enter reads it back, at your pace.'
              clear; style Elegant; type 'I loooove this (honestly). But
              maybe not. Ship it!' (45 ms a key); wait 5200 (the typing's
              own cues settle); read-back at 200 wpm; until-read; wait 600
            6 'Same words. Another performer.'
              style Caffeinated; wait 400; read-back at 200 wpm;
              until-read; wait 600
            7 'And when it deserves it: the whole stage.'
              clear; style Plain; type 'WHAT A DAY! ' (120 ms a key);
              wait 4200
            8 'Your turn.'
              clear; wait 300 (the tour ends; the text box has the focus)
          (plan script) -> the script flattened into a timeline of
            {:at-ms :scene i :step step}, each step starting when the one
            before it ends: :type lasts (count of its characters) x
            ms-per-key, :wait and :light their :ms, the rest 0;
            :until-read has no fixed length, so the timeline is a vector
            of segments and the shell starts the next segment's clock
            when the read-back is over.
          (due segment t-ms done) -> the steps of a segment that are due
            at t-ms (ms since the segment began) and not yet in done (a
            set of indexes), in order; for a :type step, the keys due so
            far: (keys-due step elapsed) -> the prefix of its text to
            have been typed.
          (caption script scene) -> its caption; (total-ms script) -> the
            tour's length not counting read-backs.
          Tests: plan's times for a small script; due and keys-due at
          several times, never skipping or repeating a step; every :type
          text in script is a valid message text; every :style a
          :ha/style; captions non-blank and under 60 characters; the
          script's length is between 25 and 60 s without read-backs.
          lab.main and index.html: the tour runs when the URL has ?tour,
          and from a 'Tour' button in the bar; never by itself otherwise.
            It drives the lab's own paths: typing sets the textarea's
            value and dispatches the same input event a key does (so
            cues, Auto's rhythm, dress and the director behave as for a
            person); :style goes through the picker; :reveal uses the
            wand path until the level is reached; :read-back and its pace
            through the same function Ctrl+Enter calls (the Pace slider
            shows the tour's wpm and is restored afterwards); :light sets
            the same light the mouse sets, moving along the phrase's
            glyphs.
            A caption bar (bottom centre, large enough to read, an
            aria-live polite region) shows the scene's caption. A 'Stop'
            button is visible throughout. Any key press, click, tap or
            Escape stops the tour at once: the scripted typing stops,
            whatever is on screen stays and is the visitor's to edit, the
            caption reads 'Your turn.' for 2 s and goes. The style and
            pace the visitor had before the tour are restored when it
            ends or is stopped; the reveal level stays where the tour
            took it.
            With reduced motion the tour does not run: the caption bar
            says 'The tour is motion. Reduced motion is on, so here is
            the lab instead.'
            window.__lab.tour() -> nil, or {scene caption segment
            running} as plain data.
          resources/site/index.html: under 'Try the typing lab', a second
            link 'Or watch a short tour' to lab/?tour (relative).
            Update site_test for the new text; the page still has no
            script and no external URL.
          e2e/lab.mjs, a new step 'tour' on /lab/?tour&debug, waiting on
            data, never on the clock: tour().scene advances 1 to 8 in
            order; in scene 1 the level is 0 and the background is paper;
            in scene 2 window.__lab.dress() has a gilt on 'the one thing'
            and a sampled frame shows its glow above 0.4; in scene 3 a
            swell cue appears in the overlay; in scene 4 the level reaches
            3; in scene 5 window.__lab.reading() becomes non-nil and then
            nil again, and the style is Elegant; in scene 6 a second
            reading runs in Caffeinated; in scene 7 a :card direction is
            placed; at the end
            tour() is nil, the textarea is empty and focused, and the
            picker shows what it showed before. Then a second run:
            during scene 2 press a key: tour() is nil within one frame,
            the text typed so far is still there, and typing a letter
            appends to it. Screenshots out/lab/tour-2.png (the gold lit, on
            paper) and out/lab/tour-5.png (mid read-back).
          docs/LAB.md: a section 'The tour'."
 :acceptance
 ["tour and site tests as in the design, on both hosts where they apply;
   `bb test` stays green"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the tour step and every existing step; the
   two tour screenshots for the foreman"
  "The final message gives the tour's measured length end to end in the
   browser check"]
 :non-goals
 ["The tour never starts unasked and records nothing; no video, no audio
   of its own (the lab's sound plays if the visitor turned it on)"
  "No change to cues, marks, gestures, pace, reading, dress, styles, the
   director, reveal rules or the renderer; do not edit the schema"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["docs/product/score.md" "NEXT.md" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
           "src/halfahead/lab/reading.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/dress.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/reveal.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/director.cljc"
           "public/lab/index.html" "resources/site/index.html"
           "src/halfahead/dev/site.clj" "test/halfahead/dev/site_test.clj"
           "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
